  ('Double Dumbbell Bent Over Row', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, a classic hip-hinged row that builds the whole back -- lats, upper back, and rear shoulders.', 'Hinge at the hips with a flat back roughly parallel to the floor, core braced; row the weight to the lower ribs by driving the elbows back; lower under control without the torso swinging.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Cyclist Thruster', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, a heels-elevated squat-to-press combination that emphasizes the quads through the squat and adds an overhead pressing finish.', 'Heels elevated, feet close together; squat down keeping the torso upright, then drive up explosively and press the load overhead in one fluid motion; lower back to the rack position under control.'),
