  ('Double Dumbbell Front Rack Split Squat', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held in the front-rack position at the shoulders, a stationary staggered-stance lower-body exercise -- builds single-leg strength and balance without the stepping motion of a lunge.', 'Take a split stance long enough that the front knee stays over the ankle at the bottom; lower straight down until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; drive through the front foot to stand.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Front Rack Squat', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held in the front-rack position at the shoulders, a foundational bend-the-knees-and-hips pattern that builds lower-body strength through the quads, glutes, and core.', 'Feet shoulder-width, toes slightly out; sit the hips back and down while keeping the chest tall; knees track over the toes; drive through the whole foot to stand.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Front Rack Step Up', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held in the front-rack position at the shoulders, a single-leg strength staple that steps fully onto an elevated surface -- builds unilateral leg strength and stability.', 'Place the whole foot on the box; drive through that heel to stand fully upright without pushing off the trailing leg; control the descent back down.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Front Rack Walking Lunge', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held in the front-rack position at the shoulders, a lunge performed continuously, stepping forward from one rep into the next -- adds a locomotion and balance demand to the standard lunge.', 'Step forward and lower until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; drive through the front leg to bring the back foot through into the next step, keeping the torso tall throughout.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Incline Bench Prone Row', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, set up on an incline bench, a row performed lying face-down on an incline bench -- removes the lower back from the equation to isolate the upper back and lats.', 'Chest supported on the bench, let the arms hang; row by driving the elbows back and squeezing the shoulder blades together; lower under control through a full stretch.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Low Hold Alternating Cossack Squat', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held low alongside the body, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Low Hold Alternating Lateral Lunge', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held low alongside the body, a frontal-plane lunge that steps out to the side while the trailing leg stays straight -- builds hip and adductor strength outside the usual forward/back plane.', 'Step out to the side and sit the hips back and down over the working leg; keep the trailing leg straight with the foot flat; keep the working knee tracking over the toes; push back through the working leg to return to center.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Low Hold Cossack Squat', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held low alongside the body, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Low Hold Lateral Lunge', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held low alongside the body, a frontal-plane lunge that steps out to the side while the trailing leg stays straight -- builds hip and adductor strength outside the usual forward/back plane.', 'Step out to the side and sit the hips back and down over the working leg; keep the trailing leg straight with the foot flat; keep the working knee tracking over the toes; push back through the working leg to return to center.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Pendlay Row', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, a bent over row performed from a dead stop on the floor each rep -- removes momentum and emphasizes strict pulling strength.', 'Hinge over with a flat back roughly parallel to the floor; pull explosively from a dead stop into the lower ribs, driving the elbows back; return the weight fully to the floor each rep.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Prone Row', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, a row performed face-down on a bench -- takes the lower back out of the movement to isolate the upper back.', 'Chest supported, let the arms hang fully; row by driving the elbows back and squeezing the shoulder blades together; lower under control through a full stretch.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Romanian Deadlift', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, a fundamental hip-hinge lift that picks a load up off the floor -- builds total-body pulling strength through the posterior chain.', 'Set the hips back with a flat back and the bar/handles close to the shins; brace the core before pulling; drive through the floor and extend the hips to stand tall, then reverse the motion under control.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Seated Good Morning', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, a seated hip-hinge variation that removes the legs from the movement to isolate the lower back and hips.', 'Sitting tall on a bench, hinge forward from the hips keeping the back flat; feel a stretch through the lower back and hamstrings; return to tall sitting by extending the hips.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Seesaw Bent Over Row', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, an alternating single-arm row performed from a bent-over bilateral stance -- one side rows while the other holds the bottom position, adding a core anti-rotation demand.', 'Hinge at the hips with a flat back; row one weight up to the ribs while the other stays extended at the bottom under control; alternate sides without letting the torso twist.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Staggered Stance Romanian Deadlift', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, a deadlift performed from a staggered foot position -- adds a single-leg emphasis and balance demand to the hinge pattern.', 'Stagger the feet with most of the weight on the front leg; hinge at the hips keeping the back flat; drive through the front leg to stand, keeping the back foot mainly for balance.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Suitcase Alternating Curtsy Lunge', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, a rotational lunge that steps one leg diagonally behind the other -- targets the glutes (especially glute medius) through a diagonal plane.', 'Step one leg diagonally behind and across the body, lowering the back knee toward the floor; keep the front knee tracking over the toes and the torso upright; push through the front leg to return to standing.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Suitcase Alternating Forward Lunge', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, a staggered-stance lunge that steps forward into a split position -- builds single-leg strength and challenges balance through momentum.', 'Step forward and lower straight down until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the front knee tracking over the foot, not caving in; push back off the front foot to return to standing.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Suitcase Alternating Lateral Lunge', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, a frontal-plane lunge that steps out to the side while the trailing leg stays straight -- builds hip and adductor strength outside the usual forward/back plane.', 'Step out to the side and sit the hips back and down over the working leg; keep the trailing leg straight with the foot flat; keep the working knee tracking over the toes; push back through the working leg to return to center.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Suitcase Alternating Reverse Lunge', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, a staggered-stance lunge that steps backward into a split position -- generally easier to control than a forward lunge and gentler on the front knee.', 'Step straight back and lower under control until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the torso tall and the front knee tracking over the foot; drive through the front heel to return to standing.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Suitcase Alternating Russian Step Up', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, an explosive step-up that drives the trailing leg up and forward off the box rather than just standing tall -- builds single-leg power.', 'Drive hard through the working leg on the box to bring the trailing knee up and slightly forward explosively; control the landing back down and reset before the next rep.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Suitcase Alternating Step Up', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, a single-leg strength staple that steps fully onto an elevated surface -- builds unilateral leg strength and stability.', 'Place the whole foot on the box; drive through that heel to stand fully upright without pushing off the trailing leg; control the descent back down.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Suitcase Curtsy Lunge', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, a rotational lunge that steps one leg diagonally behind the other -- targets the glutes (especially glute medius) through a diagonal plane.', 'Step one leg diagonally behind and across the body, lowering the back knee toward the floor; keep the front knee tracking over the toes and the torso upright; push through the front leg to return to standing.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Suitcase Cyclist Squat', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, a narrow-stance, heels-elevated squat that emphasizes the quads by allowing a very upright torso and deep knee bend.', 'Heels elevated (plate, wedge, or shoes), feet close together; sit straight down keeping the torso upright; let the knees travel forward over the toes; drive through the front of the foot to stand.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Suitcase Deadlift', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, a deadlift performed with the load at one or both sides of the body (like picking up a suitcase) -- adds an anti-lateral-flexion core demand.', 'Stand the load beside the feet; hinge the hips back with a flat back to grip it; drive through the floor to stand tall while resisting leaning toward the load; lower back under control.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Suitcase Deficit Split Squat', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, a split squat performed with the front foot elevated on a small platform -- increases the range of motion and demand on the front leg.', 'Front foot on a small platform, back foot on the floor behind; lower straight down through an extended range under control; drive through the front foot to stand.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Suitcase Foot Elevated Knee Over Toe Split Squat', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, a split squat variation that deliberately lets the front knee travel forward past the toes -- builds knee and ankle resilience through a deeper range.', 'Take a shorter stance than a normal split squat; let the front knee travel forward over and past the toes as you lower, keeping the heel down; control the descent and drive back up through the front leg.'),
  ('Double Dumbbell Suitcase Forward Lunge', 'Holding a dumbbell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, a staggered-stance lunge that steps forward into a split position -- builds single-leg strength and challenges balance through momentum.', 'Step forward and lower straight down until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the front knee tracking over the foot, not caving in; push back off the front foot to return to standing.'),
