  ('Double Kettlebell Mountain Climber', 'Holding a kettlebell in each hand, a dynamic core and conditioning exercise that drives the knees toward the chest from a plank position.', 'Set up in a strong high plank; drive one knee toward the chest and quickly switch legs, keeping the hips level and core braced throughout; keep a controlled pace so form doesn''t break down.'),
  ('Double Kettlebell Otis Up', 'Holding a kettlebell in each hand, a get-up-style flow move that presses the weight overhead from lying and rolls up to standing (or a chosen partial range) while keeping the arm locked out -- builds shoulder stability and total-body coordination.', 'Press the weight overhead first and keep the arm locked out through the whole movement; roll and stand up (or move through the chosen segment) without letting the weight drift from directly over the shoulder; reverse under control.'),
  ('Double Kettlebell Outside Swing', 'Holding a kettlebell in each hand, a single-arm kettlebell swing performed alongside the body rather than between the legs -- adds an anti-rotation demand to the swing.', 'Hike the bell back beside the hip; snap the hips forward to swing it up to chest height, keeping the shoulders square; control the bell back down alongside the body.'),
