  ('Double Kettlebell Suitcase Forward Lunge', 'Holding a kettlebell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, a staggered-stance lunge that steps forward into a split position -- builds single-leg strength and challenges balance through momentum.', 'Step forward and lower straight down until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the front knee tracking over the foot, not caving in; push back off the front foot to return to standing.'),
  ('Double Kettlebell Suitcase Knee Over Toe Split Squat', 'Holding a kettlebell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, a split squat variation that deliberately lets the front knee travel forward past the toes -- builds knee and ankle resilience through a deeper range.', 'Take a shorter stance than a normal split squat; let the front knee travel forward over and past the toes as you lower, keeping the heel down; control the descent and drive back up through the front leg.'),
  ('Double Kettlebell Suitcase Lateral Lunge', 'Holding a kettlebell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, a frontal-plane lunge that steps out to the side while the trailing leg stays straight -- builds hip and adductor strength outside the usual forward/back plane.', 'Step out to the side and sit the hips back and down over the working leg; keep the trailing leg straight with the foot flat; keep the working knee tracking over the toes; push back through the working leg to return to center.'),
  ('Double Kettlebell Suitcase Reverse Lunge', 'Holding a kettlebell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, a staggered-stance lunge that steps backward into a split position -- generally easier to control than a forward lunge and gentler on the front knee.', 'Step straight back and lower under control until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the torso tall and the front knee tracking over the foot; drive through the front heel to return to standing.'),
  ('Double Kettlebell Suitcase Russian Step Up', 'Holding a kettlebell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, an explosive step-up that drives the trailing leg up and forward off the box rather than just standing tall -- builds single-leg power.', 'Drive hard through the working leg on the box to bring the trailing knee up and slightly forward explosively; control the landing back down and reset before the next rep.'),
  ('Double Kettlebell Suitcase Split Squat', 'Holding a kettlebell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, a stationary staggered-stance lower-body exercise -- builds single-leg strength and balance without the stepping motion of a lunge.', 'Take a split stance long enough that the front knee stays over the ankle at the bottom; lower straight down until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; drive through the front foot to stand.'),
  ('Double Kettlebell Suitcase Step Up', 'Holding a kettlebell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, a single-leg strength staple that steps fully onto an elevated surface -- builds unilateral leg strength and stability.', 'Place the whole foot on the box; drive through that heel to stand fully upright without pushing off the trailing leg; control the descent back down.'),
  ('Double Kettlebell Suitcase Walking Lunge', 'Holding a kettlebell in each hand, held down at your side like a suitcase, a lunge performed continuously, stepping forward from one rep into the next -- adds a locomotion and balance demand to the standard lunge.', 'Step forward and lower until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; drive through the front leg to bring the back foot through into the next step, keeping the torso tall throughout.'),
  ('Double Kettlebell Sumo Deadlift', 'Holding a kettlebell in each hand, a wide-stance deadlift that shifts some of the work onto the inner thighs and shortens the range of motion for the back.', 'Wide stance with toes turned out, hands inside the knees; keep the chest up and back flat as you push the floor away; drive the hips forward to lock out at the top.'),
  ('Double Kettlebell Thruster', 'Holding a kettlebell in each hand, a full-body squat-to-press combination that builds power by linking the legs to an overhead press.', 'Hold the load at the shoulders; squat down keeping the torso upright; drive up explosively through the legs and press the load overhead in one fluid motion; return to the rack position under control.'),
  ('Dumbbell Crush Grip Bent Over Row', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), pinched end-to-end between the palms, a classic hip-hinged row that builds the whole back -- lats, upper back, and rear shoulders.', 'Hinge at the hips with a flat back roughly parallel to the floor, core braced; row the weight to the lower ribs by driving the elbows back; lower under control without the torso swinging.'),
  ('Dumbbell Crush Grip Front Rack Squat', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), held in the front-rack position at the shoulders, a foundational bend-the-knees-and-hips pattern that builds lower-body strength through the quads, glutes, and core.', 'Feet shoulder-width, toes slightly out; sit the hips back and down while keeping the chest tall; knees track over the toes; drive through the whole foot to stand.'),
  ('Dumbbell Crush Grip Otis Up', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), pinched end-to-end between the palms, a get-up-style flow move that presses the weight overhead from lying and rolls up to standing (or a chosen partial range) while keeping the arm locked out -- builds shoulder stability and total-body coordination.', 'Press the weight overhead first and keep the arm locked out through the whole movement; roll and stand up (or move through the chosen segment) without letting the weight drift from directly over the shoulder; reverse under control.'),
  ('Dumbbell Crush Grip Romanian Deadlift', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), pinched end-to-end between the palms, a fundamental hip-hinge lift that picks a load up off the floor -- builds total-body pulling strength through the posterior chain.', 'Set the hips back with a flat back and the bar/handles close to the shins; brace the core before pulling; drive through the floor and extend the hips to stand tall, then reverse the motion under control.'),
  ('Dumbbell Crush Grip Seated Good Morning', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), pinched end-to-end between the palms, a seated hip-hinge variation that removes the legs from the movement to isolate the lower back and hips.', 'Sitting tall on a bench, hinge forward from the hips keeping the back flat; feel a stretch through the lower back and hamstrings; return to tall sitting by extending the hips.'),
  ('Dumbbell Feet Elevated Frog Pump', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a glute isolation exercise performed with the soles of the feet together and knees dropped open -- emphasizes the glutes with the hips in external rotation.', 'Lying on the back, soles of the feet together and knees dropped open; drive through the heels to lift the hips, squeezing the glutes at the top; lower under control without letting the low back arch excessively.'),
  ('Dumbbell Frog Pump', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), a glute isolation exercise performed with the soles of the feet together and knees dropped open -- emphasizes the glutes with the hips in external rotation.', 'Lying on the back, soles of the feet together and knees dropped open; drive through the heels to lift the hips, squeezing the glutes at the top; lower under control without letting the low back arch excessively.'),
  ('Dumbbell Glute Bridge', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), a foundational glute activation exercise that lifts the hips off the floor from a lying position.', 'Lying on the back, knees bent, feet flat hip-width apart; drive through the heels to lift the hips until the body forms a straight line from shoulders to knees, squeezing the glutes at the top; lower under control.'),
  ('Dumbbell Goblet Alternating Cossack Squat', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), held at the chest in a goblet hold, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
  ('Dumbbell Goblet Alternating Curtsy Lunge', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), held at the chest in a goblet hold, a rotational lunge that steps one leg diagonally behind the other -- targets the glutes (especially glute medius) through a diagonal plane.', 'Step one leg diagonally behind and across the body, lowering the back knee toward the floor; keep the front knee tracking over the toes and the torso upright; push through the front leg to return to standing.'),
  ('Dumbbell Goblet Alternating Forward Lunge', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), held at the chest in a goblet hold, a staggered-stance lunge that steps forward into a split position -- builds single-leg strength and challenges balance through momentum.', 'Step forward and lower straight down until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the front knee tracking over the foot, not caving in; push back off the front foot to return to standing.'),
