  ('Dumbbell Goblet Alternating Reverse Lunge', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), held at the chest in a goblet hold, a staggered-stance lunge that steps backward into a split position -- generally easier to control than a forward lunge and gentler on the front knee.', 'Step straight back and lower under control until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the torso tall and the front knee tracking over the foot; drive through the front heel to return to standing.'),
  ('Dumbbell Goblet Alternating Russian Step Up', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), held at the chest in a goblet hold, an explosive step-up that drives the trailing leg up and forward off the box rather than just standing tall -- builds single-leg power.', 'Drive hard through the working leg on the box to bring the trailing knee up and slightly forward explosively; control the landing back down and reset before the next rep.'),
  ('Dumbbell Goblet Alternating Step Up', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), held at the chest in a goblet hold, a single-leg strength staple that steps fully onto an elevated surface -- builds unilateral leg strength and stability.', 'Place the whole foot on the box; drive through that heel to stand fully upright without pushing off the trailing leg; control the descent back down.'),
  ('Dumbbell Goblet Carry', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), held at the chest in a goblet hold, a loaded carry that builds core bracing and upper-back posture under load.', 'Keep the weight close to the chest with both hands; brace the core and stand tall; walk with controlled steps keeping the torso upright.'),
  ('Dumbbell Goblet Cossack Squat', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), held at the chest in a goblet hold, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
