  ('Dumbbell Hip Thrust', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), a glute-focused hip extension exercise -- one of the most direct ways to load and build the glutes.', 'Shoulders supported on a bench, feet planted hip-width apart; drive through the heels to lift the hips until the body forms a straight line from shoulders to knees, squeezing the glutes hard at the top; lower under control.'),
  ('Dumbbell Incline Bench Pullover', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), set up on an incline bench, a shoulder-extension exercise that moves a weight from overhead to the chest -- builds the lats and improves overhead shoulder mobility.', 'Lying on a bench (or floor), lower the weight back overhead with a slight elbow bend, feeling a stretch through the lats; pull it back over the chest by driving through the lats, not the arms.'),
  ('Dumbbell Low Hold Alternating Cossack Squat', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), held low alongside the body, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
