  ('Dumbbell Pullover', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), a shoulder-extension exercise that moves a weight from overhead to the chest -- builds the lats and improves overhead shoulder mobility.', 'Lying on a bench (or floor), lower the weight back overhead with a slight elbow bend, feeling a stretch through the lats; pull it back over the chest by driving through the lats, not the arms.'),
  ('Dumbbell Single Leg Romanian Dedlift', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), a hip-hinge movement that loads the hamstrings and glutes through a controlled lowering and raising of the weight with soft knees.', 'Push the hips straight back while keeping a soft bend in the knees and the back flat; keep the weight close to the legs; feel the stretch through the hamstrings, then drive the hips forward to stand tall.'),
  ('EZ Bar Reverse Grip Bent Over Row', 'Using an EZ bar, gripped palms-up (reverse/underhand grip), a classic hip-hinged row that builds the whole back -- lats, upper back, and rear shoulders.', 'Hinge at the hips with a flat back roughly parallel to the floor, core braced; row the weight to the lower ribs by driving the elbows back; lower under control without the torso swinging.'),
  ('Kettlebell Bottoms Up Horn Grip Cyclist Squat', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), a narrow-stance, heels-elevated squat that emphasizes the quads by allowing a very upright torso and deep knee bend.', 'Heels elevated (plate, wedge, or shoes), feet close together; sit straight down keeping the torso upright; let the knees travel forward over the toes; drive through the front of the foot to stand.'),
  ('Kettlebell Dead Bug', 'Using a kettlebell, a core-control exercise that trains the abs to keep the spine still while the arms and legs move -- a staple anti-extension drill.', 'Lying on the back, arms up and knees bent to 90 degrees; lower one arm and the opposite leg toward the floor while pressing the low back into the ground; return and alternate sides without letting the back arch.'),
  ('Kettlebell Feet Elevated Frog Pump', 'Using a kettlebell, with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a glute isolation exercise performed with the soles of the feet together and knees dropped open -- emphasizes the glutes with the hips in external rotation.', 'Lying on the back, soles of the feet together and knees dropped open; drive through the heels to lift the hips, squeezing the glutes at the top; lower under control without letting the low back arch excessively.'),
  ('Kettlebell Feet Elevated Russian Twist', 'Using a kettlebell, with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a rotational core exercise performed in a seated, torso-leaned-back position -- targets the obliques through trunk rotation.', 'Lean back to a stable torso angle, feet lifted or grounded; rotate the torso (and load, if used) from side to side under control, keeping the rotation coming from the trunk, not just the arms.'),
