  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Alternating Lateral Lunge', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), a frontal-plane lunge that steps out to the side while the trailing leg stays straight -- builds hip and adductor strength outside the usual forward/back plane.', 'Step out to the side and sit the hips back and down over the working leg; keep the trailing leg straight with the foot flat; keep the working knee tracking over the toes; push back through the working leg to return to center.'),
  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Alternating Reverse Lunge', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), a staggered-stance lunge that steps backward into a split position -- generally easier to control than a forward lunge and gentler on the front knee.', 'Step straight back and lower under control until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the torso tall and the front knee tracking over the foot; drive through the front heel to return to standing.'),
  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Alternating Russian Step Up', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), an explosive step-up that drives the trailing leg up and forward off the box rather than just standing tall -- builds single-leg power.', 'Drive hard through the working leg on the box to bring the trailing knee up and slightly forward explosively; control the landing back down and reset before the next rep.'),
  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Alternating Step Up', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), a single-leg strength staple that steps fully onto an elevated surface -- builds unilateral leg strength and stability.', 'Place the whole foot on the box; drive through that heel to stand fully upright without pushing off the trailing leg; control the descent back down.'),
  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Carry', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), a walking exercise under load that builds total-body bracing, grip, and posture.', 'Stand tall with the shoulders back and core braced before moving; take controlled steps, resisting any lean, shrug, or twist; set the load down under control at the end.'),
  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Cossack Squat', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Curtsy Lunge', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), a rotational lunge that steps one leg diagonally behind the other -- targets the glutes (especially glute medius) through a diagonal plane.', 'Step one leg diagonally behind and across the body, lowering the back knee toward the floor; keep the front knee tracking over the toes and the torso upright; push through the front leg to return to standing.'),
  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Cyclist Squat', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), a narrow-stance, heels-elevated squat that emphasizes the quads by allowing a very upright torso and deep knee bend.', 'Heels elevated (plate, wedge, or shoes), feet close together; sit straight down keeping the torso upright; let the knees travel forward over the toes; drive through the front of the foot to stand.'),
  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Foot Elevated Cossack Squat', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Foot Elevated Knee Over Toe Split Squat', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), a split squat variation that deliberately lets the front knee travel forward past the toes -- builds knee and ankle resilience through a deeper range.', 'Take a shorter stance than a normal split squat; let the front knee travel forward over and past the toes as you lower, keeping the heel down; control the descent and drive back up through the front leg.'),
  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Forward Lunge', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), a staggered-stance lunge that steps forward into a split position -- builds single-leg strength and challenges balance through momentum.', 'Step forward and lower straight down until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the front knee tracking over the foot, not caving in; push back off the front foot to return to standing.'),
  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Knee Over Toe Split Squat', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), a split squat variation that deliberately lets the front knee travel forward past the toes -- builds knee and ankle resilience through a deeper range.', 'Take a shorter stance than a normal split squat; let the front knee travel forward over and past the toes as you lower, keeping the heel down; control the descent and drive back up through the front leg.'),
  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Lateral Lunge', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), a frontal-plane lunge that steps out to the side while the trailing leg stays straight -- builds hip and adductor strength outside the usual forward/back plane.', 'Step out to the side and sit the hips back and down over the working leg; keep the trailing leg straight with the foot flat; keep the working knee tracking over the toes; push back through the working leg to return to center.'),
  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Otis Up', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), a get-up-style flow move that presses the weight overhead from lying and rolls up to standing (or a chosen partial range) while keeping the arm locked out -- builds shoulder stability and total-body coordination.', 'Press the weight overhead first and keep the arm locked out through the whole movement; roll and stand up (or move through the chosen segment) without letting the weight drift from directly over the shoulder; reverse under control.'),
  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Reverse Lunge', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), a staggered-stance lunge that steps backward into a split position -- generally easier to control than a forward lunge and gentler on the front knee.', 'Step straight back and lower under control until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the torso tall and the front knee tracking over the foot; drive through the front heel to return to standing.'),
  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Russian Step Up', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), an explosive step-up that drives the trailing leg up and forward off the box rather than just standing tall -- builds single-leg power.', 'Drive hard through the working leg on the box to bring the trailing knee up and slightly forward explosively; control the landing back down and reset before the next rep.'),
  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Split Squat', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), a stationary staggered-stance lower-body exercise -- builds single-leg strength and balance without the stepping motion of a lunge.', 'Take a split stance long enough that the front knee stays over the ankle at the bottom; lower straight down until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; drive through the front foot to stand.'),
  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Squat', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), a foundational bend-the-knees-and-hips pattern that builds lower-body strength through the quads, glutes, and core.', 'Feet shoulder-width, toes slightly out; sit the hips back and down while keeping the chest tall; knees track over the toes; drive through the whole foot to stand.'),
  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Step Up', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), a single-leg strength staple that steps fully onto an elevated surface -- builds unilateral leg strength and stability.', 'Place the whole foot on the box; drive through that heel to stand fully upright without pushing off the trailing leg; control the descent back down.'),
  ('Kettlebell Horn Grip Walking Lunge', 'Using a kettlebell, gripped by the horns (bottoms-up style), a lunge performed continuously, stepping forward from one rep into the next -- adds a locomotion and balance demand to the standard lunge.', 'Step forward and lower until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; drive through the front leg to bring the back foot through into the next step, keeping the torso tall throughout.'),
  ('Kettlebell Low Hold Alternating Cossack Squat', 'Using a kettlebell, held low alongside the body, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
  ('Kettlebell Low Hold Alternating Lateral Lunge', 'Using a kettlebell, held low alongside the body, a frontal-plane lunge that steps out to the side while the trailing leg stays straight -- builds hip and adductor strength outside the usual forward/back plane.', 'Step out to the side and sit the hips back and down over the working leg; keep the trailing leg straight with the foot flat; keep the working knee tracking over the toes; push back through the working leg to return to center.'),
  ('Kettlebell Low Hold Cossack Squat', 'Using a kettlebell, held low alongside the body, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
  ('Kettlebell Low Hold Foot Elevated Cossack Squat', 'Using a kettlebell, held low alongside the body, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
  ('Kettlebell Romanian Deadlift', 'Using a kettlebell, a fundamental hip-hinge lift that picks a load up off the floor -- builds total-body pulling strength through the posterior chain.', 'Set the hips back with a flat back and the bar/handles close to the shins; brace the core before pulling; drive through the floor and extend the hips to stand tall, then reverse the motion under control.'),
  ('Kettlebell Russian Twist', 'Using a kettlebell, a rotational core exercise performed in a seated, torso-leaned-back position -- targets the obliques through trunk rotation.', 'Lean back to a stable torso angle, feet lifted or grounded; rotate the torso (and load, if used) from side to side under control, keeping the rotation coming from the trunk, not just the arms.'),
  ('Kettlebell Start Stop Swing', 'Using a kettlebell, a kettlebell swing performed with a dead-stop pause between reps -- removes momentum and reinforces the hip-hinge pattern.', 'Hike the bell back between the legs like a hinge; snap the hips forward to swing it to chest height; let it settle to a dead stop on the ground before the next rep.'),
  ('Kettlebell Sumo Deadlift', 'Using a kettlebell, a wide-stance deadlift that shifts some of the work onto the inner thighs and shortens the range of motion for the back.', 'Wide stance with toes turned out, hands inside the knees; keep the chest up and back flat as you push the floor away; drive the hips forward to lock out at the top.'),
  ('Kettlebell Swing', 'Using a kettlebell, a ballistic hip-hinge exercise that builds explosive hip power -- the hips do the work, not the arms or back.', 'Hike the weight back like a hinge, keeping the back flat; snap the hips forward explosively to swing it up to roughly chest height; let momentum bring it back down and absorb it into the next hinge.'),
  ('Landmine Goblet Alternating Lateral Lunge', 'Using a landmine-anchored bar, held at the chest in a goblet hold, a frontal-plane lunge that steps out to the side while the trailing leg stays straight -- builds hip and adductor strength outside the usual forward/back plane.', 'Step out to the side and sit the hips back and down over the working leg; keep the trailing leg straight with the foot flat; keep the working knee tracking over the toes; push back through the working leg to return to center.'),
  ('Landmine Goblet Alternating Reverse Lunge', 'Using a landmine-anchored bar, held at the chest in a goblet hold, a staggered-stance lunge that steps backward into a split position -- generally easier to control than a forward lunge and gentler on the front knee.', 'Step straight back and lower under control until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the torso tall and the front knee tracking over the foot; drive through the front heel to return to standing.'),
  ('Landmine Goblet Cyclist Squat', 'Using a landmine-anchored bar, held at the chest in a goblet hold, a narrow-stance, heels-elevated squat that emphasizes the quads by allowing a very upright torso and deep knee bend.', 'Heels elevated (plate, wedge, or shoes), feet close together; sit straight down keeping the torso upright; let the knees travel forward over the toes; drive through the front of the foot to stand.'),
  ('Landmine Goblet Split Squat', 'Using a landmine-anchored bar, held at the chest in a goblet hold, a stationary staggered-stance lower-body exercise -- builds single-leg strength and balance without the stepping motion of a lunge.', 'Take a split stance long enough that the front knee stays over the ankle at the bottom; lower straight down until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; drive through the front foot to stand.'),
  ('Landmine Goblet Squat', 'Using a landmine-anchored bar, held at the chest in a goblet hold, a foundational bend-the-knees-and-hips pattern that builds lower-body strength through the quads, glutes, and core.', 'Feet shoulder-width, toes slightly out; sit the hips back and down while keeping the chest tall; knees track over the toes; drive through the whole foot to stand.'),
  ('Landmine Low Hold Alternating Lateral Lunge', 'Using a landmine-anchored bar, held low alongside the body, a frontal-plane lunge that steps out to the side while the trailing leg stays straight -- builds hip and adductor strength outside the usual forward/back plane.', 'Step out to the side and sit the hips back and down over the working leg; keep the trailing leg straight with the foot flat; keep the working knee tracking over the toes; push back through the working leg to return to center.'),
  ('Landmine Low Hold Lateral Lunge', 'Using a landmine-anchored bar, held low alongside the body, a frontal-plane lunge that steps out to the side while the trailing leg stays straight -- builds hip and adductor strength outside the usual forward/back plane.', 'Step out to the side and sit the hips back and down over the working leg; keep the trailing leg straight with the foot flat; keep the working knee tracking over the toes; push back through the working leg to return to center.'),
  ('Landmine Romanian Deadlift', 'Using a landmine-anchored bar, a fundamental hip-hinge lift that picks a load up off the floor -- builds total-body pulling strength through the posterior chain.', 'Set the hips back with a flat back and the bar/handles close to the shins; brace the core before pulling; drive through the floor and extend the hips to stand tall, then reverse the motion under control.'),
  ('Landmine Russian Twist', 'Using a landmine-anchored bar, a rotational core exercise performed in a seated, torso-leaned-back position -- targets the obliques through trunk rotation.', 'Lean back to a stable torso angle, feet lifted or grounded; rotate the torso (and load, if used) from side to side under control, keeping the rotation coming from the trunk, not just the arms.'),
  ('Landmine Thruster', 'Using a landmine-anchored bar, a full-body squat-to-press combination that builds power by linking the legs to an overhead press.', 'Hold the load at the shoulders; squat down keeping the torso upright; drive up explosively through the legs and press the load overhead in one fluid motion; return to the rack position under control.'),
  ('Landmine V Grip Row', 'Using a landmine-anchored bar, gripped on a close, neutral V-grip handle, a pulling exercise that draws the load toward the torso -- builds the back, rear shoulders, and biceps.', 'Set the shoulder blades back and down before pulling; drive the elbow(s) back to bring the load to the torso, squeezing the back at the top; control the return through a full stretch.'),
  ('Macebell Barbarian Alternating Forward Lunge', 'Using a macebell, a staggered-stance lunge that steps forward into a split position -- builds single-leg strength and challenges balance through momentum.', 'Let the macebell''s offset weight swing naturally through its arc rather than muscling it -- control comes from timing, not brute force. Step forward and lower straight down until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the front knee tracking over the foot, not caving in; push back off the front foot to return to standing.'),
  ('Macebell Barbarian Forward Lunge', 'Using a macebell, a staggered-stance lunge that steps forward into a split position -- builds single-leg strength and challenges balance through momentum.', 'Let the macebell''s offset weight swing naturally through its arc rather than muscling it -- control comes from timing, not brute force. Step forward and lower straight down until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the front knee tracking over the foot, not caving in; push back off the front foot to return to standing.'),
  ('Macebell Barbarian Squat', 'Using a macebell, a squat performed holding the load balanced across the front of the shoulders (the clubbell/macebell "barbarian" hold), which challenges front-rack shoulder stability along with the legs.', 'Let the macebell''s offset weight swing naturally through its arc rather than muscling it -- control comes from timing, not brute force. Rest the implement across the front of both shoulders, elbows in front of the body; sit the hips back and down keeping the torso tall so the load stays balanced; drive up evenly through both feet.'),
  ('Macebell Offset Bent Over Row', 'Using a macebell, held off to one side of the body, a classic hip-hinged row that builds the whole back -- lats, upper back, and rear shoulders.', 'Let the macebell''s offset weight swing naturally through its arc rather than muscling it -- control comes from timing, not brute force. Hinge at the hips with a flat back roughly parallel to the floor, core braced; row the weight to the lower ribs by driving the elbows back; lower under control without the torso swinging.'),
  ('Macebell Order Alternating Cossack Squat', 'Using a macebell, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Let the macebell''s offset weight swing naturally through its arc rather than muscling it -- control comes from timing, not brute force. Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
