  ('Macebell Order Alternating Russian Step Up', 'Using a macebell, an explosive step-up that drives the trailing leg up and forward off the box rather than just standing tall -- builds single-leg power.', 'Let the macebell''s offset weight swing naturally through its arc rather than muscling it -- control comes from timing, not brute force. Drive hard through the working leg on the box to bring the trailing knee up and slightly forward explosively; control the landing back down and reset before the next rep.'),
  ('Macebell Order Alternating Step Up', 'Using a macebell, a single-leg strength staple that steps fully onto an elevated surface -- builds unilateral leg strength and stability.', 'Let the macebell''s offset weight swing naturally through its arc rather than muscling it -- control comes from timing, not brute force. Place the whole foot on the box; drive through that heel to stand fully upright without pushing off the trailing leg; control the descent back down.'),
  ('Macebell Order Cossack Squat', 'Using a macebell, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Let the macebell''s offset weight swing naturally through its arc rather than muscling it -- control comes from timing, not brute force. Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
