  ('Macebell Order Russian Step Up', 'Using a macebell, an explosive step-up that drives the trailing leg up and forward off the box rather than just standing tall -- builds single-leg power.', 'Let the macebell''s offset weight swing naturally through its arc rather than muscling it -- control comes from timing, not brute force. Drive hard through the working leg on the box to bring the trailing knee up and slightly forward explosively; control the landing back down and reset before the next rep.'),
  ('Macebell Order Split Squat', 'Using a macebell, a stationary staggered-stance lower-body exercise -- builds single-leg strength and balance without the stepping motion of a lunge.', 'Let the macebell''s offset weight swing naturally through its arc rather than muscling it -- control comes from timing, not brute force. Take a split stance long enough that the front knee stays over the ankle at the bottom; lower straight down until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; drive through the front foot to stand.'),
  ('Macebell Order Squat', 'Using a macebell, a squat performed holding the clubbell/macebell in the "order" position (upright at the shoulder) -- adds an asymmetric core-stability demand on top of the squat.', 'Let the macebell''s offset weight swing naturally through its arc rather than muscling it -- control comes from timing, not brute force. Keep the implement stacked vertically at the shoulder without letting it drift forward or out to the side; sit the hips back and down keeping the torso tall; brace the core to resist the pull of the offset load.'),
  ('Macebell Order Step Up', 'Using a macebell, a single-leg strength staple that steps fully onto an elevated surface -- builds unilateral leg strength and stability.', 'Let the macebell''s offset weight swing naturally through its arc rather than muscling it -- control comes from timing, not brute force. Place the whole foot on the box; drive through that heel to stand fully upright without pushing off the trailing leg; control the descent back down.'),
