  ('Macebell Reverse Grip Offset Bent Over Row', 'Using a macebell, held off to one side of the body, a classic hip-hinged row that builds the whole back -- lats, upper back, and rear shoulders.', 'Let the macebell''s offset weight swing naturally through its arc rather than muscling it -- control comes from timing, not brute force. Hinge at the hips with a flat back roughly parallel to the floor, core braced; row the weight to the lower ribs by driving the elbows back; lower under control without the torso swinging.'),
  ('Medicine Ball Alternating Single Leg V Up', 'Using a medicine ball, a single-leg V-up that alternates sides, reaching the opposite hand toward the raised foot -- adds a rotational and coordination demand to the V-up. Alternate sides each rep without resetting between them.', 'Lying flat, simultaneously raise one leg and the opposite arm to meet in the middle; lower under control and alternate sides, keeping the low back from arching.'),
  ('Medicine Ball Feet Elevated Russian Twist', 'Using a medicine ball, with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a rotational core exercise performed in a seated, torso-leaned-back position -- targets the obliques through trunk rotation.', 'Lean back to a stable torso angle, feet lifted or grounded; rotate the torso (and load, if used) from side to side under control, keeping the rotation coming from the trunk, not just the arms.'),
  ('Medicine Ball Otis Up', 'Using a medicine ball, a get-up-style flow move that presses the weight overhead from lying and rolls up to standing (or a chosen partial range) while keeping the arm locked out -- builds shoulder stability and total-body coordination.', 'Press the weight overhead first and keep the arm locked out through the whole movement; roll and stand up (or move through the chosen segment) without letting the weight drift from directly over the shoulder; reverse under control.'),
  ('Medicine Ball Russian Twist', 'Using a medicine ball, a rotational core exercise performed in a seated, torso-leaned-back position -- targets the obliques through trunk rotation.', 'Lean back to a stable torso angle, feet lifted or grounded; rotate the torso (and load, if used) from side to side under control, keeping the rotation coming from the trunk, not just the arms.'),
  ('Medicine Ball V Up', 'Using a medicine ball, a full-body core exercise that folds the body into a V, bringing the hands toward the feet.', 'Lying flat, simultaneously raise the legs and torso to meet in a V shape, reaching hands toward feet; lower under control without letting the low back slam down.'),
  ('Miniband 3 Way Cha Cha', 'Using a mini resistance band, a rhythmic lateral band-walking drill (step side, together, side) that keeps continuous tension on the hips while adding a coordination/agility element.', 'Keep a slight squat and band tension throughout; step side-together-side in a controlled rhythm, keeping the torso tall; repeat in both directions.'),
  ('Miniband Ankle Lateral Walk', 'Using a mini resistance band, a lateral band walk that steps sideways against band resistance -- targets the outer hips (glute medius) directly.', 'Sit into a slight squat with the band around the ankles or knees; step directly sideways keeping tension on the band the whole time; keep the torso tall and steps controlled.'),
  ('Miniband Ankle Monster Walk', 'Using a mini resistance band, a lateral band walk in a mini-squat stance that keeps continuous tension on the hips through both abduction and stability.', 'Sit into a slight squat with a band around the ankles or knees; step diagonally out to the side keeping tension on the band throughout; keep the torso tall and avoid bouncing.'),
  ('Miniband Ankle Side Lying Hip Abduction', 'Using a mini resistance band, a side-lying isolation exercise that lifts the top leg straight up to target the outer hip (glute medius).', 'Lying on your side, stack the hips and shoulders; lift the top leg straight up without letting the hips or torso roll back; lower under control.'),
  ('Miniband Bench Seated Hip Abduction', 'Using a mini resistance band, a seated exercise pressing the knees outward against resistance -- isolates the outer hip/glute medius.', 'Sit tall with the band or machine pad at the knees; press the knees outward against the resistance, squeezing the outer hips; return under control.'),
  ('Miniband Bicycle Crunch', 'Using a mini resistance band, a rotational core exercise that brings opposite elbow to opposite knee -- targets the obliques along with the rest of the abs.', 'Hands lightly behind the head, knees bent off the floor; rotate to bring one elbow toward the opposite knee while extending the other leg; alternate under control without pulling on the neck.'),
  ('Miniband Dead Bug', 'Using a mini resistance band, a core-control exercise that trains the abs to keep the spine still while the arms and legs move -- a staple anti-extension drill.', 'Lying on the back, arms up and knees bent to 90 degrees; lower one arm and the opposite leg toward the floor while pressing the low back into the ground; return and alternate sides without letting the back arch.'),
  ('Miniband Feet Elevated Frog Pump', 'Using a mini resistance band, with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a glute isolation exercise performed with the soles of the feet together and knees dropped open -- emphasizes the glutes with the hips in external rotation.', 'Lying on the back, soles of the feet together and knees dropped open; drive through the heels to lift the hips, squeezing the glutes at the top; lower under control without letting the low back arch excessively.'),
  ('Miniband Feet Elevated Glute Bridge', 'Using a mini resistance band, with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a foundational glute activation exercise that lifts the hips off the floor from a lying position.', 'Lying on the back, knees bent, feet flat hip-width apart; drive through the heels to lift the hips until the body forms a straight line from shoulders to knees, squeezing the glutes at the top; lower under control.'),
  ('Miniband Fire Hydrant', 'Using a mini resistance band, a hands-and-knees exercise that lifts the bent leg out to the side -- targets the outer hip/glute medius.', 'From hands and knees, keep the knee bent at roughly 90 degrees; lift the leg out to the side without rotating the hips or arching the back; lower under control.'),
  ('Miniband Frog Pump', 'Using a mini resistance band, a glute isolation exercise performed with the soles of the feet together and knees dropped open -- emphasizes the glutes with the hips in external rotation.', 'Lying on the back, soles of the feet together and knees dropped open; drive through the heels to lift the hips, squeezing the glutes at the top; lower under control without letting the low back arch excessively.'),
  ('Miniband Glute Bridge', 'Using a mini resistance band, a foundational glute activation exercise that lifts the hips off the floor from a lying position.', 'Lying on the back, knees bent, feet flat hip-width apart; drive through the heels to lift the hips until the body forms a straight line from shoulders to knees, squeezing the glutes at the top; lower under control.'),
  ('Miniband Glute Bridge Hip Abduction', 'Using a mini resistance band, a foundational glute activation exercise that lifts the hips off the floor from a lying position.', 'Lying on the back, knees bent, feet flat hip-width apart; drive through the heels to lift the hips until the body forms a straight line from shoulders to knees, squeezing the glutes at the top; lower under control.'),
  ('Miniband Hip Thrust', 'Using a mini resistance band, a glute-focused hip extension exercise -- one of the most direct ways to load and build the glutes.', 'Shoulders supported on a bench, feet planted hip-width apart; drive through the heels to lift the hips until the body forms a straight line from shoulders to knees, squeezing the glutes hard at the top; lower under control.'),
  ('Miniband Kneeling Side Plank Clamshell', 'Using a mini resistance band, from a kneeling position, a side plank combined with a hip-abduction (clamshell) movement of the top leg -- loads the obliques and glute medius together.', 'Hold a side plank with the hips lifted and level; open the top knee like a clamshell while keeping the hips stacked and stable; close under control and repeat.'),
  ('Miniband Quadruped Hip Extension', 'Using a mini resistance band, a hands-and-knees exercise ("donkey kick") that extends the leg up and back -- isolates the glutes.', 'From hands and knees, keep the knee bent at roughly 90 degrees; drive the foot up toward the ceiling by squeezing the glute, without arching the low back; lower under control.'),
  ('Miniband Romanian Deadlift', 'Using a mini resistance band, a fundamental hip-hinge lift that picks a load up off the floor -- builds total-body pulling strength through the posterior chain.', 'Set the hips back with a flat back and the bar/handles close to the shins; brace the core before pulling; drive through the floor and extend the hips to stand tall, then reverse the motion under control.'),
  ('Miniband Side Lying Clamshell', 'Using a mini resistance band, a side-lying hip exercise that opens the top knee like a clamshell -- a staple for isolating the glute medius.', 'Lying on your side with hips and knees bent, feet together; open the top knee like a clamshell, keeping the hips stacked and still; close under control.'),
  ('Miniband Single Leg Hip Thrust', 'Using a mini resistance band, a single-leg hip extension that isolates one glute at a time and adds a stability challenge.', 'Shoulders on the bench (or ground), one foot planted, the other leg extended or held up; drive through the planted heel to lift the hips, squeezing the glute at the top; lower under control.'),
  ('Miniband Standing Glute Kickback', 'Using a mini resistance band, a standing exercise that extends one leg back against resistance -- isolates the glutes with a standing-balance demand.', 'Stand tall on the support leg, slight forward lean from the hips; kick the working leg straight back squeezing the glute; return under control without arching the low back.'),
  ('Miniband Standing Hip Abduction', 'Using a mini resistance band, a standing exercise that lifts one leg out to the side against resistance -- targets the outer hip while challenging standing-leg balance.', 'Stand tall on the support leg; lift the working leg straight out to the side without leaning the torso to compensate; lower under control.'),
  ('Miniband Thigh In and Out Squat Jump', 'Using a mini resistance band, an explosive squat that leaves the ground, building lower-body power on top of squat strength.', 'Load into a shallow-to-moderate squat; drive explosively through the floor to jump; land softly by re-bending the knees and hips to absorb the impact before the next rep.'),
  ('Miniband Thigh Kneeling Side Plank Hip Abduction', 'Using a mini resistance band, from a kneeling position, a side plank combined with lifting the top leg straight -- loads the obliques and glute medius/minimus together.', 'Hold a side plank with hips lifted and stacked; lift the top leg straight up without letting the hips rotate or drop; lower under control and repeat.'),
  ('Miniband Thigh Lateral Walk', 'Using a mini resistance band, a lateral band walk that steps sideways against band resistance -- targets the outer hips (glute medius) directly.', 'Sit into a slight squat with the band around the ankles or knees; step directly sideways keeping tension on the band the whole time; keep the torso tall and steps controlled.'),
  ('Miniband Thigh Monster Walk', 'Using a mini resistance band, a lateral band walk in a mini-squat stance that keeps continuous tension on the hips through both abduction and stability.', 'Sit into a slight squat with a band around the ankles or knees; step diagonally out to the side keeping tension on the band throughout; keep the torso tall and avoid bouncing.'),
  ('Miniband Thigh Side Plank Hip Abduction', 'Using a mini resistance band, a side plank combined with lifting the top leg straight -- loads the obliques and glute medius/minimus together.', 'Hold a side plank with hips lifted and stacked; lift the top leg straight up without letting the hips rotate or drop; lower under control and repeat.'),
  ('Miniband Wall Sit Hip Abduction', 'Using a mini resistance band, an isometric hold in the bottom squat position against a wall -- builds quad endurance and positional strength.', 'Back flat against the wall, thighs roughly parallel to the floor, knees over the ankles; keep the core braced and breathe steadily through the hold.'),
  ('Parallette Mountain Climber', 'Using parallettes, a dynamic core and conditioning exercise that drives the knees toward the chest from a plank position.', 'Set up in a strong high plank; drive one knee toward the chest and quickly switch legs, keeping the hips level and core braced throughout; keep a controlled pace so form doesn''t break down.'),
  ('Parallette Plank', 'Using parallettes, a plank performed gripping parallettes -- allows a slightly deeper shoulder position and adds a grip/wrist-friendly variation.', 'Grip the parallettes directly beneath the shoulders, body in a straight line from head to heels; brace the core and hold steady without the hips sagging.'),
  ('Plate Dead Bug', 'Using a weight plate, a core-control exercise that trains the abs to keep the spine still while the arms and legs move -- a staple anti-extension drill.', 'Lying on the back, arms up and knees bent to 90 degrees; lower one arm and the opposite leg toward the floor while pressing the low back into the ground; return and alternate sides without letting the back arch.'),
  ('Plate Feet Elevated Frog Pump', 'Using a weight plate, with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a glute isolation exercise performed with the soles of the feet together and knees dropped open -- emphasizes the glutes with the hips in external rotation.', 'Lying on the back, soles of the feet together and knees dropped open; drive through the heels to lift the hips, squeezing the glutes at the top; lower under control without letting the low back arch excessively.'),
  ('Plate Feet Elevated Russian Twist', 'Using a weight plate, with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a rotational core exercise performed in a seated, torso-leaned-back position -- targets the obliques through trunk rotation.', 'Lean back to a stable torso angle, feet lifted or grounded; rotate the torso (and load, if used) from side to side under control, keeping the rotation coming from the trunk, not just the arms.'),
  ('Plate Frog Pump', 'Using a weight plate, a glute isolation exercise performed with the soles of the feet together and knees dropped open -- emphasizes the glutes with the hips in external rotation.', 'Lying on the back, soles of the feet together and knees dropped open; drive through the heels to lift the hips, squeezing the glutes at the top; lower under control without letting the low back arch excessively.'),
  ('Plate Hip Thrust', 'Using a weight plate, a glute-focused hip extension exercise -- one of the most direct ways to load and build the glutes.', 'Shoulders supported on a bench, feet planted hip-width apart; drive through the heels to lift the hips until the body forms a straight line from shoulders to knees, squeezing the glutes hard at the top; lower under control.'),
  ('Plate Otis Up', 'Using a weight plate, a get-up-style flow move that presses the weight overhead from lying and rolls up to standing (or a chosen partial range) while keeping the arm locked out -- builds shoulder stability and total-body coordination.', 'Press the weight overhead first and keep the arm locked out through the whole movement; roll and stand up (or move through the chosen segment) without letting the weight drift from directly over the shoulder; reverse under control.'),
  ('Plate Russian Twist', 'Using a weight plate, a rotational core exercise performed in a seated, torso-leaned-back position -- targets the obliques through trunk rotation.', 'Lean back to a stable torso angle, feet lifted or grounded; rotate the torso (and load, if used) from side to side under control, keeping the rotation coming from the trunk, not just the arms.'),
  ('Plate Side Lying Bent Knee Hip Abduction', 'Using a weight plate, a side-lying isolation exercise that lifts the top leg straight up to target the outer hip (glute medius).', 'Lying on your side, stack the hips and shoulders; lift the top leg straight up without letting the hips or torso roll back; lower under control.'),
  ('Resistance Band Low Row', 'Using a resistance band, a band-resisted seated-style row pulled from a low angle -- targets the mid-back with continuous tension.', 'Sit or stand tall, arms extended toward the anchor; row the handles to the ribs by driving the elbows straight back and squeezing the shoulder blades together; return under control.'),
  ('Resistance Band Mid Row', 'Using a resistance band, a band-resisted row pulled from chest height -- targets the mid-back and rear shoulders with continuous tension.', 'Stand tall facing the anchor, arms extended; row the handles to the ribs by driving the elbows back and squeezing the shoulder blades together; return under control.'),
  ('Ring Body Saw', 'Using gymnastics rings, a plank variation that slides the body forward and back through the shoulders -- adds an anti-extension challenge on top of the static plank.', 'Set up in a forearm plank with feet on sliders (or rings); push the body back and pull forward through the shoulders while keeping the hips level and core braced throughout.'),
  ('Ring Bulgarian Row', 'Using gymnastics rings, a ring row variation performed with the feet elevated (often on rings) to increase the bodyweight loading on the back.', 'Set the body in a straight line from shoulders to feet; pull the chest to the handles by driving the elbows back and squeezing the shoulder blades together; lower under control.'),
  ('Ring Eccentric Pull Up', 'Using gymnastics rings, a pull-up focused entirely on the slow lowering phase -- builds pulling strength when a full unassisted pull-up isn''t there yet.', 'Start at the top (jump or step up if needed) with the chin over the bar; lower as slowly as possible, resisting the descent the whole way down; reset and repeat.'),
  ('Ring Plank', 'Using gymnastics rings, a plank performed with the hands on gymnastics rings -- the instability adds a shoulder-stability demand to the basic plank.', 'Hands on the rings directly beneath the shoulders, body in a straight line; brace the core and keep the rings from wobbling excessively; hold steady.'),
  ('Ring Row', 'Using gymnastics rings, a bodyweight row performed on gymnastics rings -- the instability of the rings adds a stabilization demand to the basic inverted row.', 'Set the body in a straight line, heels dug in for stability; pull the chest toward the hands by driving the elbows back; lower under control keeping the core braced.'),
  ('Sandbag Back Rack Alternating Cossack Squat', 'Using a sandbag, held across the upper back, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
  ('Sandbag Back Rack Alternating Curtsy Lunge', 'Using a sandbag, held across the upper back, a rotational lunge that steps one leg diagonally behind the other -- targets the glutes (especially glute medius) through a diagonal plane.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Step one leg diagonally behind and across the body, lowering the back knee toward the floor; keep the front knee tracking over the toes and the torso upright; push through the front leg to return to standing.'),
  ('Sandbag Back Rack Alternating Russian Step Up', 'Using a sandbag, held across the upper back, an explosive step-up that drives the trailing leg up and forward off the box rather than just standing tall -- builds single-leg power.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Drive hard through the working leg on the box to bring the trailing knee up and slightly forward explosively; control the landing back down and reset before the next rep.'),
  ('Sandbag Back Rack Alternating Step Up', 'Using a sandbag, held across the upper back, a single-leg strength staple that steps fully onto an elevated surface -- builds unilateral leg strength and stability.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Place the whole foot on the box; drive through that heel to stand fully upright without pushing off the trailing leg; control the descent back down.'),
  ('Sandbag Back Rack Bulgarian Split Squat', 'Using a sandbag, held across the upper back, a rear-foot-elevated split squat -- one of the most effective single-leg strength builders, with the back foot elevated to increase range and front-leg demand.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Rear foot up on a bench, front foot far enough forward that the knee stays over the ankle; lower straight down under control; drive through the front heel to stand, keeping most of the weight on the front leg.'),
  ('Sandbag Back Rack Cossack Squat', 'Using a sandbag, held across the upper back, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
  ('Sandbag Back Rack Curtsy Lunge', 'Using a sandbag, held across the upper back, a rotational lunge that steps one leg diagonally behind the other -- targets the glutes (especially glute medius) through a diagonal plane.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Step one leg diagonally behind and across the body, lowering the back knee toward the floor; keep the front knee tracking over the toes and the torso upright; push through the front leg to return to standing.'),
  ('Sandbag Back Rack Foot Elevated Cossack Squat', 'Using a sandbag, held across the upper back, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
  ('Sandbag Back Rack Low Switch Cossack Squat', 'Using a sandbag, held across the upper back, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
  ('Sandbag Back Rack Russian Step Up', 'Using a sandbag, held across the upper back, an explosive step-up that drives the trailing leg up and forward off the box rather than just standing tall -- builds single-leg power.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Drive hard through the working leg on the box to bring the trailing knee up and slightly forward explosively; control the landing back down and reset before the next rep.'),
  ('Sandbag Back Rack Split Squat', 'Using a sandbag, held across the upper back, a stationary staggered-stance lower-body exercise -- builds single-leg strength and balance without the stepping motion of a lunge.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Take a split stance long enough that the front knee stays over the ankle at the bottom; lower straight down until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; drive through the front foot to stand.'),
  ('Sandbag Back Rack Squat', 'Using a sandbag, held across the upper back, a foundational bend-the-knees-and-hips pattern that builds lower-body strength through the quads, glutes, and core.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Feet shoulder-width, toes slightly out; sit the hips back and down while keeping the chest tall; knees track over the toes; drive through the whole foot to stand.'),
  ('Sandbag Back Rack Step Up', 'Using a sandbag, held across the upper back, a single-leg strength staple that steps fully onto an elevated surface -- builds unilateral leg strength and stability.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Place the whole foot on the box; drive through that heel to stand fully upright without pushing off the trailing leg; control the descent back down.'),
  ('Sandbag Back Rack Walking Lunge', 'Using a sandbag, held across the upper back, a lunge performed continuously, stepping forward from one rep into the next -- adds a locomotion and balance demand to the standard lunge.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Step forward and lower until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; drive through the front leg to bring the back foot through into the next step, keeping the torso tall throughout.'),
  ('Sandbag Bent Over Row', 'Using a sandbag, a classic hip-hinged row that builds the whole back -- lats, upper back, and rear shoulders.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Hinge at the hips with a flat back roughly parallel to the floor, core braced; row the weight to the lower ribs by driving the elbows back; lower under control without the torso swinging.'),
  ('Sandbag Front Rack Alternating Cossack Squat', 'Using a sandbag, held in the front-rack position at the shoulders, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
  ('Sandbag Front Rack Alternating Curtsy Lunge', 'Using a sandbag, held in the front-rack position at the shoulders, a rotational lunge that steps one leg diagonally behind the other -- targets the glutes (especially glute medius) through a diagonal plane.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Step one leg diagonally behind and across the body, lowering the back knee toward the floor; keep the front knee tracking over the toes and the torso upright; push through the front leg to return to standing.'),
  ('Sandbag Front Rack Alternating Forward Lunge', 'Using a sandbag, held in the front-rack position at the shoulders, a staggered-stance lunge that steps forward into a split position -- builds single-leg strength and challenges balance through momentum.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Step forward and lower straight down until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the front knee tracking over the foot, not caving in; push back off the front foot to return to standing.'),
  ('Sandbag Front Rack Alternating Lateral Lunge', 'Using a sandbag, held in the front-rack position at the shoulders, a frontal-plane lunge that steps out to the side while the trailing leg stays straight -- builds hip and adductor strength outside the usual forward/back plane.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Step out to the side and sit the hips back and down over the working leg; keep the trailing leg straight with the foot flat; keep the working knee tracking over the toes; push back through the working leg to return to center.'),
  ('Sandbag Front Rack Alternating Reverse Lunge', 'Using a sandbag, held in the front-rack position at the shoulders, a staggered-stance lunge that steps backward into a split position -- generally easier to control than a forward lunge and gentler on the front knee.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Step straight back and lower under control until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the torso tall and the front knee tracking over the foot; drive through the front heel to return to standing.'),
  ('Sandbag Front Rack Alternating Russian Step Up', 'Using a sandbag, held in the front-rack position at the shoulders, an explosive step-up that drives the trailing leg up and forward off the box rather than just standing tall -- builds single-leg power.', 'Expect the sandbag''s shifting weight to add an extra stability demand compared to a rigid implement. Drive hard through the working leg on the box to bring the trailing knee up and slightly forward explosively; control the landing back down and reset before the next rep.'),
