  ('Single Arm Dumbbell Front Rack Contralateral Forward Lunge', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), held in the front-rack position at the shoulders, a staggered-stance lunge that steps forward into a split position -- builds single-leg strength and challenges balance through momentum. The load is on the opposite side from the working leg, which raises the anti-rotation/anti-lateral-flexion demand on the core.', 'Step forward and lower straight down until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the front knee tracking over the foot, not caving in; push back off the front foot to return to standing.'),
