  ('Single Arm Dumbbell Front Rack Contralateral Reverse Lunge', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), held in the front-rack position at the shoulders, a staggered-stance lunge that steps backward into a split position -- generally easier to control than a forward lunge and gentler on the front knee. The load is on the opposite side from the working leg, which raises the anti-rotation/anti-lateral-flexion demand on the core.', 'Step straight back and lower under control until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the torso tall and the front knee tracking over the foot; drive through the front heel to return to standing.'),
  ('Single Arm Dumbbell Front Rack Contralateral Russian Step Up', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), held in the front-rack position at the shoulders, an explosive step-up that drives the trailing leg up and forward off the box rather than just standing tall -- builds single-leg power. The load is on the opposite side from the working leg, which raises the anti-rotation/anti-lateral-flexion demand on the core.', 'Drive hard through the working leg on the box to bring the trailing knee up and slightly forward explosively; control the landing back down and reset before the next rep.'),
