  ('Single Arm Dumbbell Suitcase Contralateral Step Up', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), held down at your side like a suitcase, a single-leg strength staple that steps fully onto an elevated surface -- builds unilateral leg strength and stability. The load is on the opposite side from the working leg, which raises the anti-rotation/anti-lateral-flexion demand on the core.', 'Place the whole foot on the box; drive through that heel to stand fully upright without pushing off the trailing leg; control the descent back down.'),
