  ('Single Arm Dumbbell Suitcase Deadlift', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), held down at your side like a suitcase, a deadlift performed with the load at one or both sides of the body (like picking up a suitcase) -- adds an anti-lateral-flexion core demand. Working one side at a time adds an anti-rotation core demand on top of the base movement.', 'Stand the load beside the feet; hinge the hips back with a flat back to grip it; drive through the floor to stand tall while resisting leaning toward the load; lower back under control.'),
