  ('Single Arm Dumbbell Suitcase Walking Lunge', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), held down at your side like a suitcase, a lunge performed continuously, stepping forward from one rep into the next -- adds a locomotion and balance demand to the standard lunge. Working one side at a time adds an anti-rotation core demand on top of the base movement.', 'Step forward and lower until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; drive through the front leg to bring the back foot through into the next step, keeping the torso tall throughout.'),
  ('Single Arm Dumbbell Thruster', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), a full-body squat-to-press combination that builds power by linking the legs to an overhead press. Working one side at a time adds an anti-rotation core demand on top of the base movement.', 'Hold the load at the shoulders; squat down keeping the torso upright; drive up explosively through the legs and press the load overhead in one fluid motion; return to the rack position under control.'),
  ('Single Arm Kettlebell Around the World', 'Using a kettlebell, a kettlebell flow drill that circles the bell around the body at the waist -- builds grip, shoulder stability, and core control through a moving target. Working one side at a time adds an anti-rotation core demand on top of the base movement.', 'Pass the bell around the waist from hand to hand, keeping the core braced and the torso still; keep the pace controlled and even in both directions.'),
  ('Single Arm Kettlebell Bent Over Row', 'Using a kettlebell, a classic hip-hinged row that builds the whole back -- lats, upper back, and rear shoulders. Working one side at a time adds an anti-rotation core demand on top of the base movement.', 'Hinge at the hips with a flat back roughly parallel to the floor, core braced; row the weight to the lower ribs by driving the elbows back; lower under control without the torso swinging.'),
  ('Single Arm Kettlebell Cyclist Thruster', 'Using a kettlebell, a heels-elevated squat-to-press combination that emphasizes the quads through the squat and adds an overhead pressing finish. Working one side at a time adds an anti-rotation core demand on top of the base movement.', 'Heels elevated, feet close together; squat down keeping the torso upright, then drive up explosively and press the load overhead in one fluid motion; lower back to the rack position under control.'),
  ('Single Arm Kettlebell Front Rack Alternating Cossack Squat', 'Using a kettlebell, held in the front-rack position at the shoulders, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength. Working one side at a time adds an anti-rotation core demand on top of the base movement.', 'Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
