  ('Single Arm Kettlebell Front Rack Alternating Reverse Lunge', 'Using a kettlebell, held in the front-rack position at the shoulders, a staggered-stance lunge that steps backward into a split position -- generally easier to control than a forward lunge and gentler on the front knee. Working one side at a time adds an anti-rotation core demand on top of the base movement.', 'Step straight back and lower under control until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the torso tall and the front knee tracking over the foot; drive through the front heel to return to standing.'),
  ('Single Arm Kettlebell Front Rack Carry', 'Using a kettlebell, held in the front-rack position at the shoulders, a loaded carry that builds core and upper-back bracing strength while walking under load. Working one side at a time adds an anti-rotation core demand on top of the base movement.', 'Keep the elbows up and the load tight to the body; brace the core hard and stand tall; walk with controlled steps, resisting any lean or twist.'),
  ('Single Arm Kettlebell Front Rack Contralateral Cossack Squat', 'Using a kettlebell, held in the front-rack position at the shoulders, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength. The load is on the opposite side from the working leg, which raises the anti-rotation/anti-lateral-flexion demand on the core.', 'Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
