  ('Single Arm Kettlebell Front Rack Foot Elevated Contralateral Knee Over Toe Split Squat', 'Using a kettlebell, held in the front-rack position at the shoulders, a split squat variation that deliberately lets the front knee travel forward past the toes -- builds knee and ankle resilience through a deeper range. The load is on the opposite side from the working leg, which raises the anti-rotation/anti-lateral-flexion demand on the core.', 'Take a shorter stance than a normal split squat; let the front knee travel forward over and past the toes as you lower, keeping the heel down; control the descent and drive back up through the front leg.'),
