  ('Slider Clubbell Order Lateral Lunge', 'Using a clubbell, a frontal-plane lunge that steps out to the side while the trailing leg stays straight -- builds hip and adductor strength outside the usual forward/back plane.', 'Let the clubbell''s offset weight swing naturally through its arc rather than muscling it -- control comes from timing, not brute force. Step out to the side and sit the hips back and down over the working leg; keep the trailing leg straight with the foot flat; keep the working knee tracking over the toes; push back through the working leg to return to center.'),
