  ('Slider Macebell Order Curtsy Lunge', 'Using a macebell, a rotational lunge that steps one leg diagonally behind the other -- targets the glutes (especially glute medius) through a diagonal plane.', 'Let the macebell''s offset weight swing naturally through its arc rather than muscling it -- control comes from timing, not brute force. Step one leg diagonally behind and across the body, lowering the back knee toward the floor; keep the front knee tracking over the toes and the torso upright; push through the front leg to return to standing.'),
