  ('Slider Macebell Order Reverse Lunge', 'Using a macebell, a staggered-stance lunge that steps backward into a split position -- generally easier to control than a forward lunge and gentler on the front knee.', 'Let the macebell''s offset weight swing naturally through its arc rather than muscling it -- control comes from timing, not brute force. Step straight back and lower under control until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the torso tall and the front knee tracking over the foot; drive through the front heel to return to standing.'),
  ('Slider Mountain Climber', 'Using sliders (or a towel/paper plate on a smooth floor), a dynamic core and conditioning exercise that drives the knees toward the chest from a plank position.', 'Set up in a strong high plank; drive one knee toward the chest and quickly switch legs, keeping the hips level and core braced throughout; keep a controlled pace so form doesn''t break down.'),
