  ('Slider Suspension Lateral Lunge', 'Using a suspension trainer, a frontal-plane lunge that steps out to the side while the trailing leg stays straight -- builds hip and adductor strength outside the usual forward/back plane.', 'Step out to the side and sit the hips back and down over the working leg; keep the trailing leg straight with the foot flat; keep the working knee tracking over the toes; push back through the working leg to return to center.'),
  ('Slider Suspension Reverse Lunge', 'Using a suspension trainer, a staggered-stance lunge that steps backward into a split position -- generally easier to control than a forward lunge and gentler on the front knee.', 'Step straight back and lower under control until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the torso tall and the front knee tracking over the foot; drive through the front heel to return to standing.'),
  ('Stability Ball Bent Knee Reverse Hyperextension', 'Using a stability ball, a posterior-chain exercise that raises the legs from a hip-supported position -- builds the glutes, hamstrings, and lower back with the spine in a neutral, decompressed position.', 'Hips supported at the edge of a bench with the legs hanging; squeeze the glutes and hamstrings to raise the legs to hip height without arching the lower back; lower under control.'),
  ('Stability Ball Body Saw', 'Using a stability ball, a plank variation that slides the body forward and back through the shoulders -- adds an anti-extension challenge on top of the static plank.', 'Set up in a forearm plank with feet on sliders (or rings); push the body back and pull forward through the shoulders while keeping the hips level and core braced throughout.'),
  ('Stability Ball Cable Russian Twist', 'Using a cable machine, a rotational core exercise performed in a seated, torso-leaned-back position -- targets the obliques through trunk rotation.', 'Lean back to a stable torso angle, feet lifted or grounded; rotate the torso (and load, if used) from side to side under control, keeping the rotation coming from the trunk, not just the arms.'),
  ('Stability Ball Crunch', 'Using a stability ball, a basic core-flexion exercise that curls the upper torso toward the pelvis.', 'Knees bent, feet flat; curl the shoulders up off the floor using the abs rather than pulling on the neck; lower under control.'),
  ('Stability Ball Dead Bug', 'Using a stability ball, a core-control exercise that trains the abs to keep the spine still while the arms and legs move -- a staple anti-extension drill.', 'Lying on the back, arms up and knees bent to 90 degrees; lower one arm and the opposite leg toward the floor while pressing the low back into the ground; return and alternate sides without letting the back arch.'),
  ('Stability Ball Dumbbell Hip Thrust', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), a glute-focused hip extension exercise -- one of the most direct ways to load and build the glutes.', 'Shoulders supported on a bench, feet planted hip-width apart; drive through the heels to lift the hips until the body forms a straight line from shoulders to knees, squeezing the glutes hard at the top; lower under control.'),
  ('Stability Ball Dumbbell Pullover', 'Using a dumbbell (or a pair), a shoulder-extension exercise that moves a weight from overhead to the chest -- builds the lats and improves overhead shoulder mobility.', 'Lying on a bench (or floor), lower the weight back overhead with a slight elbow bend, feeling a stretch through the lats; pull it back over the chest by driving through the lats, not the arms.'),
  ('Stability Ball Feet Elevated Crunch', 'Using a stability ball, with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a basic core-flexion exercise that curls the upper torso toward the pelvis.', 'Knees bent, feet flat; curl the shoulders up off the floor using the abs rather than pulling on the neck; lower under control.'),
  ('Stability Ball Feet Elevated Frog Pump', 'Using a stability ball, with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a glute isolation exercise performed with the soles of the feet together and knees dropped open -- emphasizes the glutes with the hips in external rotation.', 'Lying on the back, soles of the feet together and knees dropped open; drive through the heels to lift the hips, squeezing the glutes at the top; lower under control without letting the low back arch excessively.'),
  ('Stability Ball Feet Elevated Glute Bridge', 'Using a stability ball, with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a foundational glute activation exercise that lifts the hips off the floor from a lying position.', 'Lying on the back, knees bent, feet flat hip-width apart; drive through the heels to lift the hips until the body forms a straight line from shoulders to knees, squeezing the glutes at the top; lower under control.'),
  ('Stability Ball Feet Elevated Oblique Crunch', 'Using a stability ball, with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a side-focused crunch that targets the obliques through lateral flexion.', 'Lying on the back or side, crunch up and to the side rather than straight forward; feel the contraction through the side of the waist; lower under control.'),
  ('Stability Ball Feet Elevated Plank', 'Using a stability ball, with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a core-bracing hold that builds anti-extension and total-body tension.', 'Set up on forearms or hands with the body in a straight line from head to heels; brace the core and squeeze the glutes; keep the hips from sagging or piking up.'),
  ('Stability Ball Feet Elevated Russian Twist', 'Using a stability ball, with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a rotational core exercise performed in a seated, torso-leaned-back position -- targets the obliques through trunk rotation.', 'Lean back to a stable torso angle, feet lifted or grounded; rotate the torso (and load, if used) from side to side under control, keeping the rotation coming from the trunk, not just the arms.'),
  ('Stability Ball Forearm Plank', 'Using a stability ball, a core-bracing hold on the forearms that builds anti-extension core strength.', 'Forearms on the floor, body in a straight line from head to heels; brace the core and squeeze the glutes to keep the hips from sagging or piking; breathe steadily through the hold.'),
  ('Stability Ball Frog Reverse Hyperextension', 'Using a stability ball, a reverse hyperextension performed with the knees bent and turned out (frog position), emphasizing the glutes over the hamstrings.', 'Hips at the edge of the bench, knees bent and turned out, heels together; squeeze the glutes to lift the legs, keeping the motion coming from the hips rather than the lower back; lower under control.'),
  ('Stability Ball Hamstring Curl', 'Using a stability ball, a hamstring isolation exercise that curls the heels toward the glutes.', 'Keep the hips pressed down and square throughout; curl the heels toward the glutes squeezing the hamstrings at the top; lower under control without letting the hips pike up.'),
  ('Stability Ball Hip Thrust', 'Using a stability ball, a glute-focused hip extension exercise -- one of the most direct ways to load and build the glutes.', 'Shoulders supported on a bench, feet planted hip-width apart; drive through the heels to lift the hips until the body forms a straight line from shoulders to knees, squeezing the glutes hard at the top; lower under control.'),
  ('Stability Ball Hyperextension', 'Using a stability ball, a posterior-chain exercise that raises the torso from a hip-supported position -- builds the lower back, glutes, and hamstrings.', 'Hips supported at the edge of the bench, legs anchored; lower the torso under control, then raise it back to a straight line by squeezing the glutes and hamstrings rather than yanking with the lower back.'),
  ('Stability Ball Knee Tuck', 'Using a stability ball, a core exercise (often on sliders/rings) that draws the knees in toward the chest from a plank position.', 'Set up in a strong plank with feet on sliders or a wheel; draw both knees in toward the chest while keeping the hips level; extend back out under control.'),
  ('Stability Ball Kneeling Body Saw', 'Using a stability ball, from a kneeling position, a plank variation that slides the body forward and back through the shoulders -- adds an anti-extension challenge on top of the static plank.', 'Set up in a forearm plank with feet on sliders (or rings); push the body back and pull forward through the shoulders while keeping the hips level and core braced throughout.'),
  ('Stability Ball Kneeling Rollout', 'Using a stability ball, from a kneeling position, a core-extension exercise that rolls a wheel (or the body) out from kneeling and pulls it back -- one of the more demanding anti-extension core exercises.', 'Kneeling, brace the core hard before rolling out; roll out only as far as control allows without the low back sagging; pull back in by driving through the lats and abs, not just the arms.'),
  ('Stability Ball Kneeling Stir the Pot', 'Using a stability ball, from a kneeling position, a stability-ball plank that draws small circles with the forearms -- a heavy anti-rotation/anti-extension core challenge.', 'Forearms on the ball, body in a straight plank line; draw small, controlled circles with the forearms while keeping the hips and torso still and braced.'),
  ('Stability Ball Miniband Feet Elevated Glute Bridge', 'Using a mini resistance band, with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a foundational glute activation exercise that lifts the hips off the floor from a lying position.', 'Lying on the back, knees bent, feet flat hip-width apart; drive through the heels to lift the hips until the body forms a straight line from shoulders to knees, squeezing the glutes at the top; lower under control.'),
  ('Stability Ball Oblique Crunch', 'Using a stability ball, a side-focused crunch that targets the obliques through lateral flexion.', 'Lying on the back or side, crunch up and to the side rather than straight forward; feel the contraction through the side of the waist; lower under control.'),
  ('Stability Ball Prone Cobra', 'Using a stability ball, a face-down back-extension exercise that strengthens the upper back and postural muscles.', 'Lying face down, arms out to the sides; lift the chest and arms off the floor by squeezing the shoulder blades together; lower under control.'),
  ('Stability Ball Reverse Crunch', 'Using a stability ball, a crunch variation that curls the hips and knees up toward the chest instead of the shoulders up toward the knees -- emphasizes the lower abs.', 'Lying on the back, knees bent; curl the hips off the floor bringing the knees toward the chest, using the abs rather than momentum; lower under control.'),
  ('Stability Ball Reverse Hyperextension', 'Using a stability ball, a posterior-chain exercise that raises the legs from a hip-supported position -- builds the glutes, hamstrings, and lower back with the spine in a neutral, decompressed position.', 'Hips supported at the edge of a bench with the legs hanging; squeeze the glutes and hamstrings to raise the legs to hip height without arching the lower back; lower under control.'),
  ('Stability Ball Russian Twist', 'Using a stability ball, a rotational core exercise performed in a seated, torso-leaned-back position -- targets the obliques through trunk rotation.', 'Lean back to a stable torso angle, feet lifted or grounded; rotate the torso (and load, if used) from side to side under control, keeping the rotation coming from the trunk, not just the arms.'),
  ('Stability Ball Single Leg Hip Thrust', 'Using a stability ball, a single-leg hip extension that isolates one glute at a time and adds a stability challenge.', 'Shoulders on the bench (or ground), one foot planted, the other leg extended or held up; drive through the planted heel to lift the hips, squeezing the glute at the top; lower under control.'),
  ('Stability Ball Sit Up', 'Using a stability ball, a classic core-flexion exercise that brings the torso all the way up from lying to sitting.', 'Knees bent, feet anchored or flat; curl up through the spine to a full sit-up; lower under control rather than dropping back down.'),
  ('Stability Ball Stir the Pot', 'Using a stability ball, a stability-ball plank that draws small circles with the forearms -- a heavy anti-rotation/anti-extension core challenge.', 'Forearms on the ball, body in a straight plank line; draw small, controlled circles with the forearms while keeping the hips and torso still and braced.'),
  ('Stability Ball V Up Pass', 'Using a stability ball, a full-body core exercise that folds the body into a V, bringing the hands toward the feet.', 'Lying flat, simultaneously raise the legs and torso to meet in a V shape, reaching hands toward feet; lower under control without letting the low back slam down.'),
  ('Stability Ball Wall Slide Squat', 'Using a stability ball, a squat performed with the back sliding down a wall -- a beginner-friendly way to groove the pattern with feedback on depth and torso position.', 'Back flat against the wall, feet out slightly in front; slide down under control keeping the low back in contact with the wall; stop at a comfortable depth and slide back up.'),
  ('Stability Ball Windshield Wiper', 'Using a stability ball, a rotational core exercise that sweeps the legs side to side from a lying or hanging position -- targets the obliques through end-range rotation.', 'Lift the legs (bent knees for an easier version) and lower them together to one side under control, then sweep to the other side; keep the shoulders flat on the floor throughout.'),
  ('Superband Assisted Bar Pull Up', 'Using a heavy-duty resistance band, a band-assisted pull-up that reduces bodyweight to build toward a full unassisted pull-up.', 'Set the band for just enough assistance to complete the rep with good form; pull the chin over the bar by driving the elbows down; lower under control through a full stretch.'),
  ('Superband Assisted Reverse Nordic', 'Using a heavy-duty resistance band, a quad and hip-flexor lengthening exercise that leans the torso back from a kneeling position under control -- the eccentric-focused counterpart to the Nordic curl.', 'Kneeling with the torso tall, lean back from the knees under control keeping the hips extended; go only as far as control allows and use the band assist to return to upright.'),
  ('Superband Dead Bug', 'Using a heavy-duty resistance band, a core-control exercise that trains the abs to keep the spine still while the arms and legs move -- a staple anti-extension drill.', 'Lying on the back, arms up and knees bent to 90 degrees; lower one arm and the opposite leg toward the floor while pressing the low back into the ground; return and alternate sides without letting the back arch.'),
  ('Superband Good Morning', 'Using a heavy-duty resistance band, a hip-hinge movement loaded across the back that targets the hamstrings, glutes, and lower back.', 'Soft bend in the knees, hinge the hips straight back while keeping the back flat; lower until a stretch is felt through the hamstrings, then drive the hips forward to stand tall.'),
  ('Superband Half Kneeling Pallof Press', 'Using a heavy-duty resistance band, from a half-kneeling position, an anti-rotation core exercise that presses a cable/band straight out from the chest while resisting the pull toward the anchor.', 'Stand side-on to the anchor with the band/cable at the chest; press straight out and hold, resisting the pull rotating the torso toward the anchor; return under control.'),
  ('Superband Lateral Step Hip Adduction', 'Using a heavy-duty resistance band, a lateral step combined with resisted hip adduction -- targets the inner thigh through a functional stepping pattern.', 'Step laterally against the band resistance, then draw the trailing leg back in against the band''s pull; keep the movement controlled in both directions.'),
  ('Superband Pallof Press', 'Using a heavy-duty resistance band, an anti-rotation core exercise that presses a cable/band straight out from the chest while resisting the pull toward the anchor.', 'Stand side-on to the anchor with the band/cable at the chest; press straight out and hold, resisting the pull rotating the torso toward the anchor; return under control.'),
  ('Superband Prone Bench Hamstring Curl', 'Using a heavy-duty resistance band, a hamstring isolation exercise that curls the heels toward the glutes.', 'Keep the hips pressed down and square throughout; curl the heels toward the glutes squeezing the hamstrings at the top; lower under control without letting the hips pike up.'),
  ('Superband Prone Bench Single Leg Hamstring Curl', 'Using a heavy-duty resistance band, a single-leg hamstring curl that isolates one hamstring at a time.', 'Set up face down (or supported) with one leg engaged; curl the heel toward the glute, keeping the hips pressed down and square; lower under control.'),
  ('Superband Prone Hamstring Curl', 'Using a heavy-duty resistance band, a hamstring isolation exercise that curls the heels toward the glutes.', 'Keep the hips pressed down and square throughout; curl the heels toward the glutes squeezing the hamstrings at the top; lower under control without letting the hips pike up.'),
  ('Superband Prone Single Leg Hamstring Curl', 'Using a heavy-duty resistance band, a single-leg hamstring curl that isolates one hamstring at a time.', 'Set up face down (or supported) with one leg engaged; curl the heel toward the glute, keeping the hips pressed down and square; lower under control.'),
  ('Superband Pull Through', 'Using a heavy-duty resistance band, a cable/band hip-hinge exercise pulled from between the legs -- reinforces the hip-hinge pattern with continuous tension.', 'Facing away from the anchor, hinge the hips back with a flat back, letting the cable pull through between the legs; drive the hips forward to stand tall, squeezing the glutes at the top.'),
  ('Superband Side Lying Hanging Hip Adduction', 'Using a heavy-duty resistance band, a suspension-trainer exercise that squeezes the legs together against the strap resistance -- targets the inner thighs.', 'Hold the strap between the ankles or knees; squeeze the legs together against the resistance; return under control without swinging.'),
  ('Superband Single Leg Standing Bent Knee Hip External Rotation', 'Using a heavy-duty resistance band, a standing hip-mobility/strength exercise that rotates the bent leg outward against resistance -- targets the deep hip rotators.', 'Stand tall on the support leg with the working knee bent; rotate the knee outward against the resistance keeping the hips level; return under control.'),
  ('Superband Standing Hip Adduction', 'Using a heavy-duty resistance band, a standing exercise that draws the leg in across the midline against resistance -- targets the inner thigh (adductors).', 'Stand tall on the support leg; draw the working leg across the front of the body against the resistance; return under control.'),
  ('Superband Tall Kneeling Pallof Press', 'Using a heavy-duty resistance band, from a tall-kneeling position, an anti-rotation core exercise that presses a cable/band straight out from the chest while resisting the pull toward the anchor.', 'Stand side-on to the anchor with the band/cable at the chest; press straight out and hold, resisting the pull rotating the torso toward the anchor; return under control.'),
  ('Superband Tall Kneeling Pull Through', 'Using a heavy-duty resistance band, from a tall-kneeling position, a cable/band hip-hinge exercise pulled from between the legs -- reinforces the hip-hinge pattern with continuous tension.', 'Facing away from the anchor, hinge the hips back with a flat back, letting the cable pull through between the legs; drive the hips forward to stand tall, squeezing the glutes at the top.'),
  ('Suspension Alternating Cossack Squat', 'Using a suspension trainer, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
  ('Suspension Alternating Curtsy Lunge', 'Using a suspension trainer, a rotational lunge that steps one leg diagonally behind the other -- targets the glutes (especially glute medius) through a diagonal plane.', 'Step one leg diagonally behind and across the body, lowering the back knee toward the floor; keep the front knee tracking over the toes and the torso upright; push through the front leg to return to standing.'),
  ('Suspension Alternating Lateral Lunge', 'Using a suspension trainer, a frontal-plane lunge that steps out to the side while the trailing leg stays straight -- builds hip and adductor strength outside the usual forward/back plane.', 'Step out to the side and sit the hips back and down over the working leg; keep the trailing leg straight with the foot flat; keep the working knee tracking over the toes; push back through the working leg to return to center.'),
  ('Suspension Alternating Reverse Lunge', 'Using a suspension trainer, a staggered-stance lunge that steps backward into a split position -- generally easier to control than a forward lunge and gentler on the front knee.', 'Step straight back and lower under control until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; keep the torso tall and the front knee tracking over the foot; drive through the front heel to return to standing.'),
  ('Suspension Body Saw', 'Using a suspension trainer, a plank variation that slides the body forward and back through the shoulders -- adds an anti-extension challenge on top of the static plank.', 'Set up in a forearm plank with feet on sliders (or rings); push the body back and pull forward through the shoulders while keeping the hips level and core braced throughout.'),
  ('Suspension Cossack Squat', 'Using a suspension trainer, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
  ('Suspension Curtsy Lunge', 'Using a suspension trainer, a rotational lunge that steps one leg diagonally behind the other -- targets the glutes (especially glute medius) through a diagonal plane.', 'Step one leg diagonally behind and across the body, lowering the back knee toward the floor; keep the front knee tracking over the toes and the torso upright; push through the front leg to return to standing.'),
  ('Suspension Cyclist Squat', 'Using a suspension trainer, a narrow-stance, heels-elevated squat that emphasizes the quads by allowing a very upright torso and deep knee bend.', 'Heels elevated (plate, wedge, or shoes), feet close together; sit straight down keeping the torso upright; let the knees travel forward over the toes; drive through the front of the foot to stand.'),
  ('Suspension Feet Elevated Forearm Plank', 'Using a suspension trainer, with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a core-bracing hold on the forearms that builds anti-extension core strength.', 'Forearms on the floor, body in a straight line from head to heels; brace the core and squeeze the glutes to keep the hips from sagging or piking; breathe steadily through the hold.'),
  ('Suspension Feet Elevated Glute Bridge', 'Using a suspension trainer, with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a foundational glute activation exercise that lifts the hips off the floor from a lying position.', 'Lying on the back, knees bent, feet flat hip-width apart; drive through the heels to lift the hips until the body forms a straight line from shoulders to knees, squeezing the glutes at the top; lower under control.'),
  ('Suspension Feet Elevated Plank', 'Using a suspension trainer, with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a core-bracing hold that builds anti-extension and total-body tension.', 'Set up on forearms or hands with the body in a straight line from head to heels; brace the core and squeeze the glutes; keep the hips from sagging or piking up.'),
  ('Suspension Foot Elevated Cossack Squat', 'Using a suspension trainer, with the rear/working foot elevated to increase the range and demand, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
  ('Suspension Hamstring Curl', 'Using a suspension trainer, a hamstring isolation exercise that curls the heels toward the glutes.', 'Keep the hips pressed down and square throughout; curl the heels toward the glutes squeezing the hamstrings at the top; lower under control without letting the hips pike up.'),
  ('Suspension Knee Tuck', 'Using a suspension trainer, a core exercise (often on sliders/rings) that draws the knees in toward the chest from a plank position.', 'Set up in a strong plank with feet on sliders or a wheel; draw both knees in toward the chest while keeping the hips level; extend back out under control.'),
  ('Suspension Low Row', 'Using a suspension trainer, a band-resisted seated-style row pulled from a low angle -- targets the mid-back with continuous tension.', 'Sit or stand tall, arms extended toward the anchor; row the handles to the ribs by driving the elbows straight back and squeezing the shoulder blades together; return under control.'),
  ('Suspension Low Switch Cossack Squat', 'Using a suspension trainer, a wide-stance lateral squat that shifts weight fully onto one leg at a time -- builds hip and ankle mobility along with single-leg strength.', 'Take a wide stance, toes turned slightly out; sit the hips back and down over one leg while the other leg stays straight with the foot flat or heel lifted; keep the chest tall and the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
  ('Suspension Mid Row', 'Using a suspension trainer, a band-resisted row pulled from chest height -- targets the mid-back and rear shoulders with continuous tension.', 'Stand tall facing the anchor, arms extended; row the handles to the ribs by driving the elbows back and squeezing the shoulder blades together; return under control.'),
  ('Suspension Sissy Squat', 'Using a suspension trainer, a quad-isolation squat that hinges forward at the knees rather than the hips, keeping the torso and thighs in a straight line.', 'Rise onto the balls of the feet if able; lean back from the knees (not the hips) while keeping hips extended and torso straight; lower under control and use the hand assist only as needed to control the descent.'),
  ('Suspension Skater Squat', 'Using a suspension trainer, a single-leg squat with the rear leg held free behind the body -- builds single-leg strength and balance together.', 'Balance on one leg with the other held just off the floor behind you; sit the hips back and down while reaching the free leg back for balance; keep the loaded knee tracking over the toes.'),
  ('Suspension Split Squat', 'Using a suspension trainer, a stationary staggered-stance lower-body exercise -- builds single-leg strength and balance without the stepping motion of a lunge.', 'Take a split stance long enough that the front knee stays over the ankle at the bottom; lower straight down until both knees reach roughly 90 degrees; drive through the front foot to stand.'),
  ('Suspension Squat', 'Using a suspension trainer, a squat performed holding a suspension trainer for light assistance -- a good regression while building squat depth and confidence.', 'Hold the handles for light support only, not to pull yourself up; sit the hips back and down keeping the chest tall; use just enough assistance to complete a full-depth rep with good form.'),
  ('Tire Alternating Russian Step Up', 'Using a tire, an explosive step-up that drives the trailing leg up and forward off the box rather than just standing tall -- builds single-leg power.', 'Drive hard through the working leg on the box to bring the trailing knee up and slightly forward explosively; control the landing back down and reset before the next rep.'),
  ('Tire Alternating Step Up', 'Using a tire, a single-leg strength staple that steps fully onto an elevated surface -- builds unilateral leg strength and stability.', 'Place the whole foot on the box; drive through that heel to stand fully upright without pushing off the trailing leg; control the descent back down.'),
  ('Tire Bulgarian Split Squat', 'Using a tire, a rear-foot-elevated split squat -- one of the most effective single-leg strength builders, with the back foot elevated to increase range and front-leg demand.', 'Rear foot up on a bench, front foot far enough forward that the knee stays over the ankle; lower straight down under control; drive through the front heel to stand, keeping most of the weight on the front leg.'),
  ('Tire Feet Elevated Glute Bridge', 'Using a tire, with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a foundational glute activation exercise that lifts the hips off the floor from a lying position.', 'Lying on the back, knees bent, feet flat hip-width apart; drive through the heels to lift the hips until the body forms a straight line from shoulders to knees, squeezing the glutes at the top; lower under control.'),
  ('Tire Macebell Staggered Stance Slam', 'Using a macebell, an overhead slam performed from a staggered stance -- adds a rotational, single-leg-dominant element to the power slam.', 'Let the macebell''s offset weight swing naturally through its arc rather than muscling it -- control comes from timing, not brute force. Stagger the feet; raise the implement overhead and drive it down forcefully across the front leg, using the hips to generate power; reset and repeat, switching stance as needed.'),
  ('Tire Mountain Climber', 'Using a tire, a dynamic core and conditioning exercise that drives the knees toward the chest from a plank position.', 'Set up in a strong high plank; drive one knee toward the chest and quickly switch legs, keeping the hips level and core braced throughout; keep a controlled pace so form doesn''t break down.'),
  ('Tire Russian Step Up', 'Using a tire, an explosive step-up that drives the trailing leg up and forward off the box rather than just standing tall -- builds single-leg power.', 'Drive hard through the working leg on the box to bring the trailing knee up and slightly forward explosively; control the landing back down and reset before the next rep.'),
  ('Tire Sledge Hammer Staggered Stance Slam', 'Using a tire, an overhead slam performed from a staggered stance -- adds a rotational, single-leg-dominant element to the power slam.', 'Stagger the feet; raise the implement overhead and drive it down forcefully across the front leg, using the hips to generate power; reset and repeat, switching stance as needed.'),
  ('Tire Step Up', 'Using a tire, a single-leg strength staple that steps fully onto an elevated surface -- builds unilateral leg strength and stability.', 'Place the whole foot on the box; drive through that heel to stand fully upright without pushing off the trailing leg; control the descent back down.'),
  ('Trap Bar Bent Over Row', 'Using a trap bar, a classic hip-hinged row that builds the whole back -- lats, upper back, and rear shoulders.', 'The neutral grip and centered load make this a back-friendlier option than a straight bar for many clients. Hinge at the hips with a flat back roughly parallel to the floor, core braced; row the weight to the lower ribs by driving the elbows back; lower under control without the torso swinging.'),
  ('Trap Bar Deadlift', 'Using a trap bar, a fundamental hip-hinge lift that picks a load up off the floor -- builds total-body pulling strength through the posterior chain.', 'The neutral grip and centered load make this a back-friendlier option than a straight bar for many clients. Set the hips back with a flat back and the bar/handles close to the shins; brace the core before pulling; drive through the floor and extend the hips to stand tall, then reverse the motion under control.'),
  ('Trap Bar Pendlay Row', 'Using a trap bar, a bent over row performed from a dead stop on the floor each rep -- removes momentum and emphasizes strict pulling strength.', 'The neutral grip and centered load make this a back-friendlier option than a straight bar for many clients. Hinge over with a flat back roughly parallel to the floor; pull explosively from a dead stop into the lower ribs, driving the elbows back; return the weight fully to the floor each rep.'),
  ('Trap Bar Rack Pull', 'Using a trap bar, a partial-range deadlift pulled from roughly knee height -- overloads the top portion of the deadlift and the back/grip.', 'The neutral grip and centered load make this a back-friendlier option than a straight bar for many clients. Set the bar at the pin height, hinge the hips back slightly with a flat back; drive the hips forward to stand tall, squeezing the glutes at the top; lower under control.'),
  ('Trap Bar Romanian Deadlift', 'Using a trap bar, a fundamental hip-hinge lift that picks a load up off the floor -- builds total-body pulling strength through the posterior chain.', 'The neutral grip and centered load make this a back-friendlier option than a straight bar for many clients. Set the hips back with a flat back and the bar/handles close to the shins; brace the core before pulling; drive through the floor and extend the hips to stand tall, then reverse the motion under control.'),
  ('Trap Bar Staggered Stance Deadlift', 'Using a trap bar, a deadlift performed from a staggered foot position -- adds a single-leg emphasis and balance demand to the hinge pattern.', 'The neutral grip and centered load make this a back-friendlier option than a straight bar for many clients. Stagger the feet with most of the weight on the front leg; hinge at the hips keeping the back flat; drive through the front leg to stand, keeping the back foot mainly for balance.'),
  ('Wall Ball Body Saw', 'Using a wall ball, a plank variation that slides the body forward and back through the shoulders -- adds an anti-extension challenge on top of the static plank.', 'Set up in a forearm plank with feet on sliders (or rings); push the body back and pull forward through the shoulders while keeping the hips level and core braced throughout.'),
  ('Wall Ball Feet Elevated Russian Twist', 'Using a wall ball, with the feet elevated to increase the demand, a rotational core exercise performed in a seated, torso-leaned-back position -- targets the obliques through trunk rotation.', 'Lean back to a stable torso angle, feet lifted or grounded; rotate the torso (and load, if used) from side to side under control, keeping the rotation coming from the trunk, not just the arms.'),
  ('Wall Ball Half Kneeling Lateral Toss', 'Using a wall ball, from a half-kneeling position, a rotational power exercise that tosses a weighted ball to the side -- builds explosive hip and core rotation power.', 'Load into a slight squat, rotate away from the target then explosively rotate through to release the ball to the side; let the hips and core drive the power, not just the arms.'),
  ('Wall Ball Lateral Toss', 'Using a wall ball, a rotational power exercise that tosses a weighted ball to the side -- builds explosive hip and core rotation power.', 'Load into a slight squat, rotate away from the target then explosively rotate through to release the ball to the side; let the hips and core drive the power, not just the arms.'),
  ('Wall Ball Russian Twist', 'Using a wall ball, a rotational core exercise performed in a seated, torso-leaned-back position -- targets the obliques through trunk rotation.', 'Lean back to a stable torso angle, feet lifted or grounded; rotate the torso (and load, if used) from side to side under control, keeping the rotation coming from the trunk, not just the arms.'),
  ('Wall Ball Russian Twist Lateral Toss', 'Using a wall ball, a rotational core exercise performed in a seated, torso-leaned-back position -- targets the obliques through trunk rotation.', 'Lean back to a stable torso angle, feet lifted or grounded; rotate the torso (and load, if used) from side to side under control, keeping the rotation coming from the trunk, not just the arms.')
) as v(name, description, cues)
where lower(e.name) = lower(v.name)
  and e.client_description is null
  and e.coach_cues is null;
